+# UI5 — Baton identity and empty screens
+
+Date: 2026-10-06
+Status: complete, independently reviewed and fixture checked; ready to commit after UI4. Current shared tree passes 377 engine tests, Swift build and 79 app tests with the installed SDK flags. Earlier design explorations below are historical.
+
+## Selected compact logo
+
+Ibrahim selected burgundy/black and asked for I.A in the smaller logo. The built-in image-generation edit produced `app/Brand/baton-icon-burgundy-black-signed.png`; its identical runtime copy is `app/Sources/BatonUI/Resources/Brand/baton-icon.png`. I inspected the generated asset and its light/graphite renderings at 58/92 points; the signature is legible and clear of the handoff symbol. The light tile maintains black contrast on graphite. Previous sheets below remain design history.
+
+Final compact prompt (built-in image-generation edit mode):
+
+```text
+Use case: logo-brand.
+Asset type: production compact signed app logo for Baton, on a rounded-square light-backed tile.
+Reference: the provided burgundy/black Baton logo sheet. The user chose this identity and now wants the small "I.A" signature included in the smaller logo too.
+Primary request: extract and faithfully recreate just the compact app-icon tile at the lower right of the reference, then add the SAME handwritten "I.A" maker signature discreetly inside its bottom-right corner.
+Preserve the exact handoff emblem: upper conversation form wine burgundy #762D43; lower conversation form and diagonal baton true black #000000; original B-like silhouette, open gaps and proportions. Do not redesign the symbol.
+Composition: one square icon, no wordmark. A crisp soft-white rounded-square tile centered on a genuinely transparent canvas, a generous well-balanced central emblem, with enough lower padding for the signature. The emblem fills about 70 percent of the tile width, leaving all edges unclipped. The handwritten "I.A" is black, inset from bottom/right edges, about 14 percent of tile width, legible yet clearly secondary. The signature is a careful maker's mark, not part of the emblem and never overlaps the lower speech-tail.
+Text verbatim: "I.A". No "Baton" wordmark or other words on this compact asset.
+Flat graphic colour, no bevel, no gradients, no texture, no shadows, no extra border. High quality crisp vector-like edges. The white tile is opaque; only the surrounding outside of the rounded tile is transparent. Preserve all original logo contours.
+```
+
+
+## Burgundy and black follow-up
+
+Ibrahim asked to see burgundy with black. The built-in image-generation tool produced `app/Brand/baton-logo-burgundy-black-v4.png` with burgundy #762D43 and black #000000, preserving the handoff geometry, wordmark and I.A signature. I inspected the result: the pairing is present, the wordmark/signature are accurate, and the dark-surface examples use a light backing to keep the black part visible. This is a review treatment; direct placement of black on graphite would lose contrast and is not adopted. Palette selection remains pending. No app code, fixtures or real chats were changed; no tests were run for the image artifact.
+
+Final prompt (built-in image-generation mode):
+
+```text
+Use case: logo-brand.
+Asset type: Burgundy and black identity review sheet for Baton's approved logo.
+Reference: the supplied Baton sheet. Preserve EXACT emblem shape, the two conversation forms arranged as a B, the diagonal baton and white gaps, the wordmark "Baton", and the subtle handwritten "I.A" maker signature. Recolour and present only; do not redesign.
+User request: Burgundy and black.
+Create one beautiful landscape review sheet. Upper two thirds pale silver #E7E8EB, large primary horizontal signed logo centered: upper conversation form rich burgundy #762D43, lower form and diagonal baton true black #000000. Wordmark true black, signature true black, small beneath right edge as in reference. Clean flat graphic with crisp edges.
+Lower third graphite #50545D. On the left show the SAME burgundy-and-black emblem and wordmark inside a spacious soft-white rounded panel so that the black component remains readable on this dark app surface; do NOT recolour the black component white. On the right show one white rounded-square app tile with the exact burgundy-and-black emblem only. The maker signature appears only with the wordmark, never inside the icon tile.
+No palette labels or additional text. Text exact: "Baton", "I.A". Keep elegant spacing, accurate geometry and consistent logo throughout. Burgundy should remain visibly red-wine and distinct from black. No green/blue, no gradient, no neon, no metallic effect, no mockup device, no shadows or scene. The sheet has opaque silver and graphite backgrounds.
+```
+
+
+
+## Burgundy follow-up
+
+Ibrahim asked to explore burgundy with another colour. The built-in image-generation tool produced `app/Brand/baton-logo-burgundy-v3.png`, showing the same mark and I.A signature with champagne, silver and blush companions. I visually inspected the sheet: all three pairings preserve the identity and replace blue/green. Orchestrator recommendation: champagne for warmth and a distinct maker identity; silver is the closest fit to the current glass palette. No pairing has been selected, and no app implementation or tests were run.
+
+Final prompt:
+
+```text
