+## Request and sequence
+
+Ibrahim requested useful wording and the Baton logo in places that currently show blank content. He asked to design the logo first: descriptive, creative and modern, with a small `I.A` signature.
+
+The first stage produces a logo concept for visual review. It does not change screens, catalogue wording, app launch behavior, or real chats. Existing unstaged implementation work is preserved.
+
+## Design direction
+
+The mark depicts a handoff between two conversation forms, arranged around a central baton and a compact B silhouette. The palette comes from the existing app: slate `#20242D`, silver `#DFE6EE`, blue `#1763B5`, teal `#007B75`, and graphite `#50545D`. The wordmark is a restrained contemporary sans serif; the small `I.A` signature belongs to the signed lockup, while the icon remains legible at menu-bar size.
+
+The distinctive feature is the handoff geometry. Avoid generic chain links, AI sparkles, circuit boards or a collection of decorative effects. The empty screens will later pair the quiet mark with one concrete explanation and a relevant action, with user-facing sentences supplied through the note catalogue.
+
+## Generation prompt
+
+Built-in image generation; use case `logo-brand`. The full prompts and saved artifact paths are recorded below.
+
+## Checks and limits
+
+This stage changes design artifacts only. No engine or app tests are required for image generation. App implementation and its verification have not begun.
+
