+### Primary transparent concept
+
+```text
+Use case: logo-brand.
+Asset type: first original logo concept for Baton, a macOS app that links a conversation in one coding agent to a conversation in another and passes their history safely between them.
+Primary request: design a distinctive, sophisticated modern logo, descriptive of conversation handoff, with a subtle personal signature "I.A".
+Design: a compact original geometric emblem in which two rounded open conversation forms exchange one short diagonal baton. Their combined silhouette should suggest the letter B without becoming a literal typography exercise. The center handoff/negative space is the memorable feature. Bold simple contours, optically balanced, no tiny decorative details. It must work at menu-bar icon size in one color. Beside the emblem, an impeccably typeset wordmark "Baton" in a custom-feeling clean contemporary sans-serif with gentle round details. Place a small refined signature "I.A" discreetly below the right end of the wordmark, like a maker's signature, clearly secondary.
+Composition: one primary horizontal logo lockup, centered with generous clean transparent padding. Emblem on left, wordmark on right, signature beneath the wordmark's right edge. Do not repeat the logo or add presentation boards.
+Palette: emblem uses restrained deep teal #007B75 and blue #1763B5 to distinguish the two conversation forms; wordmark slate #20242D; signature quiet slate. Flat graphic artwork with exceptionally crisp vector-like edges, not a photograph or glossy 3D render.
+Text verbatim: "Baton", "I.A".
+Constraints: genuinely transparent background. Original mark, professional and memorable, the signature readable but small. No mockup devices, no scene, no extra text, no explanatory labels, no tagline. Avoid generic chain-link icons, infinity knots, interlocking rings, speech bubbles side-by-side without a handoff, robot heads, sparkles, circuit traces, fake bevels, and neon effects.
+```
