+```text
+Use case: logo-brand.
+Asset type: a polished visual review sheet for the provided Baton logo concept.
+Input image: the provided transparent logo is the identity reference. Preserve its specific emblem shape, wordmark lettering "Baton", and discreet handwritten "I.A" signature accurately; do not redesign the core mark.
+Primary request: make a restrained, beautifully composed brand review sheet showing this SAME identity on the existing macOS app's cool silver/light palette and graphite/dark palette, plus its standalone small app icon.
+Layout: wide landscape, immaculate quiet spacing. Upper two thirds on cool silver #DFE6EE: large primary signed horizontal logo, centered and visually balanced, teal #007B75 and blue #1763B5 emblem, slate #20242D wordmark with subtle I.A maker's signature below its right edge. Lower third is a dark graphite #50545D horizontal strip: left, the same logo with off-white wordmark/signature and teal-blue mark adapted for dark contrast; right, a single rounded-square app tile containing the mark ONLY, and to its right the SAME mark in simple monochrome at two visibly smaller sizes, proving icon readability.
+No labels, no new copy, no extra text beyond Baton and I.A. Use actual flat identity artwork and clean modern macOS-like spacing. No photo mockup, no devices, no paper textures, no decoration, no dramatic shadows. Signature belongs only to the lockups; app/menu icons have no signature or wordmark. Preserve transparent interior gaps of the original emblem. The final sheet itself has an opaque silver and graphite background.
