+### Challenge and separate review
+
+- Root's first full app check caught a real compatibility regression: adding presentation notes to the deliberately note-less links.sample fixture broke omittedPresentationNotesRemainCompatible. Restored that legacy fixture; all other applicable fixtures carry the new notes. The final suite passes.
+- Separate reviewer found the empty popover instructed use of a nonexistent sidebar. Added empty.popover title/body pointing to its existing Link a recent chat action, changed its model mapping and test expectations, and injected the notes in nonlegacy links fixtures. Reviewer rechecked and reported no remaining warnings or critical issues.
+- UI4 follow-up reviewer found the hidden-turn boundary rail ended before the first visible card. The correction is carried in UI5's overlapping SyncStatusView: group the fallback and first card in a zero-spacing wrapper with an aligned 16-point connector. The note remains outside that card to avoid attributing hidden history to a visible turn. Reviewer confirmed the gap warning resolved; empty filters still contain no reached marker.
+- Root inspected light/graphite empty-linked and filtered renderings and the signed asset. CUA inspected the native main-window selection state and filtered state. Attached had no messages or reached markers, showed its explanatory branded state, and clicking Show all turns restored Turn 3/Turn 4 and their messages. The fixture was left showing the signed filtered state for Ibrahim.
